\DOC ENSURES_WHILE_PUP_TAC

\TYPE {ENSURES_WHILE_PUP_TAC : term -> term -> term -> term -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Replaces an {ensures} goal about a loop by a single conjunctive goal containing
a nonzero-trip-count side condition together with four {ensures} subcomponents
(entry, loop body, back-edge, exit) built from a supplied loop invariant.

\DESCRIBE
The tactic takes four term arguments: a numeral-valued bound {t} giving the
number of loop iterations; two terms giving program points, namely the
body-start point and the back-edge/test address (either absolute or as an
offset); and a loop invariant of the form {\i s. ...} parameterised by the
iteration counter and the machine state. The assumptions are untouched and one
goal results, whose conclusion conjoins: {~(t = 0)}; an {ensures} from the
original precondition to the invariant at {0} at the body-start point; a clause
carrying the invariant at {x1} from the body-start point to the invariant at
{x1 + 1} at the back-edge point; a clause carrying the invariant at {x1} from
the back-edge point back to the body-start point; and an {ensures} from the
invariant at {t} at the back-edge point to the original postcondition. Every
component keeps the original frame ({MAYCHANGE} term) unchanged, and each state
predicate is conjoined with the program-loaded and program-counter conditions
taken from the original precondition.
{
   A ?- ensures ...
   ======================================================================  ENSURES_WHILE_PUP_TAC t body_start back_edge (\i s. ...)
   A ?- ~(t = 0) /\
        ensures ... /\
        (forall x1. x1 < t /\ ~(x1 = t) /\ ~(t = 0) /\ 0 < t ==> ensures ...) /\
        (forall x1. 0 < x1 /\ x1 < t /\ ~(x1 = t) /\ ~(x1 = 0) /\ ~(t = 0) /\ 0 < t
                    ==> ensures ...) /\
        ensures ...
}

\COMMENTS
The observed traces show only this single kind of transformation, on goals
whose conclusion is an {ensures} for the same machine model.

\ENDDOC
